  "chapter": {
    "number": 8,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "For the Chief Musician; on an instrument of Gath. A Psalm by David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Yahweh, our Lord, how majestic is your name in all the earth!",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "text": "You have set your glory above the heavens!",
            "poem": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "From the lips of babes and infants you have established strength,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "text": "because of your adversaries, that you might silence the enemy and the avenger.",
            "poem": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "When I consider your heavens, the work of your fingers,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "text": "the moon and the stars, which you have ordained,",
            "poem": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "what is man, that you think of him?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "text": "What is the son of man, that you care for him?",
            "poem": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For you have made him a little lower than the angels,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 7
          },
          {
            "text": "and crowned him with glory and honor.",
            "poem": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You make him ruler over the works of your hands.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "text": "You have put all things under his feet:",
            "poem": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "All sheep and cattle,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "text": "yes, and the animals of the field,",
            "poem": 2
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "the birds of the sky, the fish of the sea,",
            "poem": 2
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          },
          {
            "text": "and whatever passes through the paths of the seas.",
            "poem": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Yahweh, our Lord,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "text": "how majestic is your name in all the earth!",
            "poem": 2
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 7,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Hebrew: Elohim. The word Elohim, used here, usually means “God”, but can also mean “gods”, “princes”, or “angels”. The Septuagint reads “angels” here. See also the quote from the Septuagint in Hebrews 2:7.",
